{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nA 200 from `/health` does not establish that this container can serve an MCP request, yet it is\nall the blue-green cutover waits for. `/health` is a FastMCP `custom_route` registered\ndeliberately OUTSIDE the auth middleware and the DNS-rebinding guard (`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py`,\n`register_health_route`), and `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` polls\n`GET http://127.0.0.1:<newport>/health` until 200 and flips the nginx upstream — never issuing one\n`/mcp` request. Measured on the box 2026-08-28, a container was promoted 54 s before serving its\nfirst. A container whose `REBAR_MCP_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` does not admit the hostname real traffic\ncarries answers `/health` 200 while 421-ing every real request, and the deploy promotes it — the\nclass of `mobile-groovy-badger`.\n\n## Approach\n\nDrive one real `initialize` through this server's own `StreamableHTTPSessionManager` inside the\nASGI lifespan — after the session manager is running, before Starlette answers\n`lifespan.startup.complete` — and publish the outcome as a `handshake` object on `/health`.\nUvicorn accepts no connection until lifespan startup completes (Starlette's `Router.lifespan`\nsends that message only after entering the context), so a later `/health` 200 proves by\nconstruction that this container has already served an MCP handshake. Only that ordering buys the\nimplication, so this is no background task or lazy field.\n\n**Conclusive.** The probe calls `mcp.session_manager.handle_request(scope, receive, send)` — the\nentry point the `/mcp` route serves through (`StreamableHTTPASGIApp(self._session_manager)`,\n`mcp/server/fastmcp/server.py:970`). A 200 needs the guard to admit the Host,\n`StreamableHTTPServerTransport` to parse the body, the session manager to start a server task,\nand `Server.run` to answer the `initialize` request. A throwaway in-process probe on a `FastMCP` built\nlike `build_server`'s returned 200 in 3.0 ms admitting, 421 in 2.1 ms non-admitting. Boundary: calling the\nsession manager directly does not traverse `RequireAuthMiddleware`/`ProxyAuthMiddleware` (the\nserver holds no credential to present to itself). That is why an auth-enabled boot is\nUNAFFECTED — it reports the same truthful result (pinned by an AC), so the gate cannot freeze an\nauth-enabled deployment. This proves the transport + protocol path, not auth config.\n\n**Bounded.** The drive runs under `anyio.fail_after(budget)` with module constant\n`DEFAULT_HANDSHAKE_BUDGET_SECONDS = 10`, wrapped so a `TimeoutError`, any `Exception`, or a\nnon-200 status is a reported failure record, not a raise; boot continues. The timeout scope and\nclock are injected parameters — the `drain_then_exit(..., sleep=, monotonic=)` seam — so the bound\nis provable with a fake clock, not by sleeping.\n\n**Probe Host** (`select_probe_host`), in precedence order, from this server's OWN settings:\n(1) the host of the declared public resource URL, `mcp.settings.auth.resource_server_url`\n(`REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL`; on the box `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp`,\n`docker-compose.yml:400`), port appended only when not the scheme default — declared\nINDEPENDENTLY of the allowlist, so an allowlist admitting a DIFFERENT hostname is caught with a\n421: the deploy-promotes-a-421-container case; (2) else the first literal `allowed_hosts`\nentry (no `*`); (3) else the first `host:*` entry as `host:<bind port>`, the form `_validate_host`\nmatches (`mcp/server/transport_security.py`); (4) else the bind address,\n`0.0.0.0`/`::` -> `127.0.0.1` — where an allowlist admitting nothing usable (empty, or only\nunmatchable forms like `*.example.com`) lands, then refused by its own guard. LIMIT: with no declared\npublic resource URL the probe has nothing independent to check the allowlist against, so there a\npass proves the request path works, not that the right hosts are admitted.\n\nThe deploy gate closes like the store gate (`autodeploy.sh` 5b): after `/health` 200, refuse the\nflip when `handshake.ok` is present and false; an absent field promotes (mixed-version safety, as\nthe `store` gate treats an older container). The refusal calls `record_mcp_backoff_failure`, NOT\nthe `record_backoff_failure` 5b uses: `$BACKOFF_FILE` gates the whole script, so recording there\nwould let an mcp failure suppress the review-bot deploy (`autodeploy.sh:64-69`). 5b's own wrong\nrecorder is a separate pre-existing defect, filed as `prespinal-gem-kinkajou`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — `select_probe_host`, the ASGI `initialize` drive, the bounded\n  never-raising `run_startup_handshake`, `install_startup_handshake` (wraps\n  `app.router.lifespan_context`, unwrapping any `ProxyAuthMiddleware`), the `handshake` field on\n  `/health`, and its call from `run_http_with_grace`. 463 LOC today, under the 800 cap.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_health_startup_handshake.py` — the unit tests.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py` — pin the `handshake` key + auth case.\n- `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` — readiness gate on `handshake.ok`.\n- `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py` — deploy-gate tests on the `mcp_box` harness,\n  which stubs per-port `/health` bodies.\n\nNo new config key: the budget is a module constant, per the docstring's\n`DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS` rationale.\n\n## Testing\n\nEvery assertion is anchored: each test first proves the handshake actually RAN (a drive counter,\nor the record's presence) and only then asserts its outcome — an assertion that passes when the\nhandshake never ran is this bug restated. Both directions are covered, the bound is proved with an\ninjected clock not a sleep, and each production edit is reverted with its targeted test required\nto fail (rc checked).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A correctly configured server reports a successful startup handshake on `/health`:\n      `test_correctly_configured_server_reports_a_successful_handshake` asserts the drive counter\n      incremented, record `{\"ok\": True, \"status\": 200}`.\n- [ ] A server whose host allowlist does not admit its own probe reports the handshake failed\n      with the refusing status instead of reporting ready:\n      `test_unadmitted_probe_host_is_reported_as_failed_with_421` asserts `ok is False`,\n      `status == 421`.\n- [ ] A handshake exceeding its budget is a reported failure and boot continues:\n      `test_a_hanging_drive_is_bounded_by_the_budget` (injected clock, no sleep) asserts the call\n      returns a failure record naming the timeout.\n- [ ] A handshake whose drive raises never propagates the exception:\n      `test_a_raising_drive_is_reported_not_propagated` asserts the record carries the message,\n      the lifespan still yielding.\n- [ ] The handshake completes inside the ASGI lifespan before uvicorn accepts a connection:\n      `test_handshake_is_recorded_before_lifespan_startup_complete` drives the raw lifespan\n      protocol, asserting the record exists before `lifespan.startup.complete`.\n- [ ] An auth-enabled server still reports a successful handshake, so the gate cannot freeze its\n      deploys: `test_an_auth_enabled_server_still_reports_a_successful_handshake` asserts\n      `ok is True` with a token verifier configured.\n- [ ] The cutover refuses to promote a container reporting a failed handshake:\n      `test_failed_handshake_container_is_not_promoted` asserts `mcp-handshake-failed` logged,\n      upstream byte-identical, nginx not reloaded, container removed.\n- [ ] A container whose `/health` predates the field is still promoted (mixed-version safety):\n      `test_container_with_no_handshake_field_still_promotes` asserts the flip happens.\n- [ ] A server whose allowlist admits a hostname OTHER than its declared public resource URL\n      reports the handshake failed: `test_allowlist_that_admits_the_wrong_hostname_fails` asserts\n      `ok is False`, `status == 421`.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` exits 0.\n- [ ] The affected test modules exit 0.\n- [ ] Each production edit reverted individually makes its targeted test fail (rc checked).\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787964513703901001,"uuid":"bcd80f82-6431-4322-80bb-292c5233c505"}